      "text": "<h3><b data-rte-class=\"rte-temp\"><span class=\"fontsize-1-5em\">&quot;Current strategies treating massive irreparable rotator cuff tears often present a challenge to surgeons and may require long and frustrating rehabilitation processes for patients,” said the lead investigator in the clinical study, Dr. Nikhil Verma, M.D. “The results of the study demonstrate the InSpace balloon is a ‘game-changer’ and presents a shorter, less invasive option that may enable sustained, clinically meaningful improvements in shoulder function and symptoms.”</span></b></h3>\n<h3>—Nikhil N. Verma, M.D.</h3>\n",
